<title>MALAYSIA: SOCCER-WORLD YOUTH CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-WORLD YOUTH CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the world youth</p>
<p>soccer championship on Friday:</p>
<p>Group F</p>
<p>Ivory Coast 1 Mexico 1 (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ivory coast - Die Serg 33</p>
<p>Mexico - Eduardo Lillingston 44</p>
<p>Group E</p>
<p>Australia 1 Hungary 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Daniel Allsopp 90</p>
<p>Group D</p>
<p>Japan 6 Costa Rica 2 (3-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Japan -- Harutaka Ono 3, 21, Shunsuke Nakamura 6, Shinji</p>
<p>Jojo 75, Kenji Fukuda 89, Yuichiro Nagai 90</p>
<p>Costa Rica -- Froylan Ledezma 28, Alonso Solis 56</p>
<p>Group F</p>
<p>England 5 United Arab Emirates 0 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Daniel Murphy 7, 34, 49, Michael Owen 51, Ali Al</p>
<p>Yarees 59 own goal</p>
<p>Group E</p>
<p>Argentina 2 Canada 1 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Argentina -- Bernardo Romeo 32, Roman Riquelme 65</p>
<p>Canada -- Jason Bent 44</p>
